{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}Terms — {{ product }}{% endblock %}
{% block description %}Subscription terms for {{ product }}.{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
<main class="legal">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>Subscription terms</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated {{ today }}.</p>

    <h2>What you are buying</h2>
    <p>A subscription to a weekly email digest and CSV of operator-licence events for the
      territories you select, for your own internal business use.</p>

    <h2>What you may do with it</h2>
    <p>Use it to find and contact prospects, load it into your own CRM, and share it inside your
      own organisation.</p>

    <h2>What you may not do</h2>
    <p>Resell it, redistribute it, publish it, or use it to build or train a competing product or
      dataset. One subscription covers one organisation.</p>

    <h2>Accuracy</h2>
    <p>We derive this from public records and check it as described on the
      <a href="/">home page</a>, but it is provided <strong>as is</strong>. Verify anything you are
      about to spend money on. We are not liable for decisions you take on the basis of it, and our
      total liability is capped at what you paid us in the previous twelve months.</p>

    <h2>Your obligations when contacting people</h2>
    <p>You are the data controller for your own outreach. UK GDPR and PECR apply, and they treat
      sole traders and partnerships differently from corporate subscribers — we mark those in every
      CSV so you can route them appropriately. We are not your lawyers and this is not legal advice.</p>

    <h2>Billing and cancellation</h2>
    <p>Monthly in advance by card through Stripe, or annually at {{ pricing.annual_months }}× the
      monthly rate. Cancel any time through the billing portal; you keep access to the end of the
      period you have paid for. Founding rates are locked for {{ pricing.founding_months }} months
      from signup and then move to list price, and we will tell you before that happens.</p>

    <h2>If we get something wrong</h2>
    <p>If we ship materially wrong data we will correct it in the next digest and tell everyone
      affected. If we cannot deliver for a sustained period we will refund the affected period.</p>

    <h2>Ending it</h2>
    <p>Either of us can end the subscription at any time. If we end it without cause we refund the
      unused portion.</p>

    <h2>Law</h2>
    <p>{{ legal.jurisdiction }}</p>

    {%- if dry_run %}
    <hr>
    <p class="updated"><strong>Draft.</strong> Not reviewed by a solicitor. Have it checked before
      taking money.</p>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
</main>
{% endblock %}
